    "body": "Hello, I'm seeing similar behavior in elvish, seems like there is trouble getting the column size. I'm very new to both starship and elvish so this is the best I could do in modifying the starship.elv init:\r\n```\r\nuse re\r\n\r\nfn get-term-width { \r\n    var stty_size = (stty size </dev/tty)\r\n    put (re:find '(\\d+) (\\d+)' $stty_size)[groups][{2}][text]\r\n}\r\n\r\n# Install starship\r\nset edit:prompt = {\r\n    var cmd-duration = (printf \"%.0f\" (* $edit:command-duration 1000))\r\n    var term-width = ( get-term-width )\r\n    /opt/local/bin/starship prompt --jobs=$num-bg-jobs --cmd-duration=$cmd-duration --status=$cmd-status-code --logical-path=$pwd --terminal-width=$term-width\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI lifted the term width code from https://github.com/zzamboni/elvish-modules/blob/master/tty.org\r\n\r\nOn fish, I've noticed that even when resizing the window the prompt is able to resize along with it anyone have an idea how to achieve that with elvish?",
